IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-persons`

-- Schedules 8 and 9 of the Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376): the circumstances in which a claimant is to be
-- treated as having limited capability for work (Schedule 8, used by regulation 39(6) and (7)) and as having limited
-- capability for work and work-related activity (Schedule 9, used by regulation 40(5) and (6)).
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt, a plain-text rendering of the revised text (legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-07-16)
-- made by a converter script. It is not the official text. Every `-- src:N | ...` line copies line N of that file.
-- Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Seat: a person who claims or receives Universal Credit (see uc4-seat.l4).
--
-- Each paragraph has a record of the facts it reads and a rule that decides whether the paragraph applies.
-- The Acts and Regulations that the paragraphs cite are not among the inputs, so whether a disease or an infection is one
-- of those they describe is a stated input. Where a paragraph hands a judgment to the Secretary of State ("the Secretary of
-- State is satisfied that ..."), the judgment is a BOOLEAN input worded as the condition and is never guessed.

§ `Schedule 8 — Circumstances in which a claimant is to be treated as having limited capability for work`

-- src:2762 | SCHEDULE 8 — Circumstances in which a claimant is to be treated as having limited capability for work

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Paragraph 1 — Receiving certain treatments`

-- src:2763 | Receiving certain treatments
-- src:2764 | 1 The claimant is receiving—
-- src:2765 | (a) regular weekly treatment by way of haemodialysis for chronic renal failure;
-- src:2766 | (b) treatment by way of plasmapheresis; or
-- src:2767 | (c) regular weekly treatment by way of total parenteral nutrition for gross impairment of enteric function,
-- src:2768 | or is recovering from any of those forms of treatment in circumstances in which the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant should be treated as having limited capability for work.
@ref Sch 8 para 1 (src:2763-2768)
DECLARE `Sch 8 para 1 treatment facts` HAS
    `receiving regular weekly treatment by way of haemodialysis for chronic renal failure`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `receiving treatment by way of plasmapheresis`                                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `receiving regular weekly treatment by way of total parenteral nutrition for gross impairment of enteric function`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `recovering from any of those forms of treatment`                                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant should be treated as having limited capability for work`   IS A BOOLEAN

-- The Secretary of State's satisfaction is attached by the text to the recovering limb only ("or is recovering from any of
-- those forms of treatment in circumstances in which the Secretary of State is satisfied that ..."): fork F-sch8-1.
@ref Sch 8 para 1 (src:2763-2768)
GIVEN facts IS A `Sch 8 para 1 treatment facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 8 para 1 — receiving certain treatments` facts MEANS
    (`Sch 8 para 1 — receiving one of the listed treatments` facts)
    OR (`Sch 8 para 1 — recovering, and the Secretary of State is satisfied` facts)

@ref Sch 8 para 1(a) to (c) (src:2764-2767)
GIVEN facts IS A `Sch 8 para 1 treatment facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 8 para 1 — receiving one of the listed treatments` facts MEANS
    (facts's `receiving regular weekly treatment by way of haemodialysis for chronic renal failure`)
    OR (facts's `receiving treatment by way of plasmapheresis`)
    OR (facts's `receiving regular weekly treatment by way of total parenteral nutrition for gross impairment of enteric function`)

@ref Sch 8 para 1, closing words (src:2768)
GIVEN facts IS A `Sch 8 para 1 treatment facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 8 para 1 — recovering, and the Secretary of State is satisfied` facts MEANS
    (facts's `recovering from any of those forms of treatment`)
    AND (facts's `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant should be treated as having limited capability for work`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Paragraph 2 — In hospital`

-- src:2769 | In hospital
-- src:2770 | 2 (1) The claimant is—
-- src:2771 | (a) undergoing medical or other treatment as a patient in a hospital or similar institution; or
-- src:2772 | (b) recovering from such treatment in circumstances in which the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant should be treated as having limited capability for work.
-- src:2773 | (2) The circumstances in which a claimant is to be regarded as undergoing treatment falling within sub-paragraph (1)(a) include where the claimant is attending a residential programme of rehabilitation for the treatment of drug or alcohol dependency.
-- src:2774 | (3) For the purposes of this paragraph, a claimant is to be regarded as undergoing treatment as a patient in a hospital or similar institution only if that claimant has been advised by a health care professional to stay for a period of 24 hours or longer following medical or other treatment.
@ref Sch 8 para 2 (src:2769-2774)
DECLARE `Sch 8 para 2 hospital facts` HAS
    `undergoing medical or other treatment as a patient in a hospital or similar institution`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `attending a residential programme of rehabilitation for the treatment of drug or alcohol dependency`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `has been advised to stay for a period of 24 hours or longer following medical or other treatment`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `adviser`                                                                                                           IS A Practitioner
    `recovering from such treatment`                                                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant should be treated as having limited capability for work`     IS A BOOLEAN

-- Sub-paragraph (3) says a claimant is regarded as undergoing treatment as a patient in a hospital or similar institution
-- "only if" advised by a health care professional to stay 24 hours or longer. It is read as limiting the patient limb (1)(a)
-- and not the residential rehabilitation programme that sub-paragraph (2) says is "included" (fork F-sch8-2).
-- "Health care professional" is the keel's `reg 2 — health care professional`: this paragraph is not regulation 98.
@ref Sch 8 para 2(2) and (3) (src:2773-2774)
GIVEN facts IS A `Sch 8 para 2 hospital facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 8 para 2(2) and (3) — the claimant is regarded as undergoing treatment as a patient in a hospital or similar institution` facts MEANS
    (facts's `attending a residential programme of rehabilitation for the treatment of drug or alcohol dependency`)
    OR patient
    WHERE
        patient MEANS
            (facts's `undergoing medical or other treatment as a patient in a hospital or similar institution`)
            AND (facts's `has been advised to stay for a period of 24 hours or longer following medical or other treatment`)
            AND (`reg 2 — health care professional` (facts's adviser))

@ref Sch 8 para 2(1) (src:2770-2772)
GIVEN facts IS A `Sch 8 para 2 hospital facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 8 para 2 — in hospital` facts MEANS
    (`Sch 8 para 2(2) and (3) — the claimant is regarded as undergoing treatment as a patient in a hospital or similar institution` facts)
    OR recovering
    WHERE
        recovering MEANS
            (facts's `recovering from such treatment`)
            AND (facts's `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant should be treated as having limited capability for work`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Paragraph 3 — Prevented from working by law`

-- out of range: the public health Acts and Regulations cited in Schedule 8 (not among the inputs): whether the infection or contamination is one they describe is a stated input
-- src:2775 | Prevented from working by law
-- src:2776 | 3 (1) The claimant—
-- src:2777 | (a) is excluded or abstains from work pursuant to a request or notice in writing lawfully made or given under an enactment; or
-- src:2778 | (b) is otherwise prevented from working pursuant to an enactment,
-- src:2779 | by reason of it being known or reasonably suspected that the claimant is infected or contaminated by, or has been in contact with a case of, a relevant infection or contamination.
-- src:2780 | (2) In sub-paragraph (1) “relevant infection or contamination” means—
-- src:2781 | (a) in England and Wales—
-- src:2782 | (i) any incidence or spread of infection or contamination, within the meaning of section 45A(3) of the Public Health (Control of Disease) Act 1984 in respect of which regulations are made under Part 2A of that Act (public health protection) for the purpose of preventing, protecting against, controlling or providing a public health response to, such incidence or spread, or
-- src:2783 | (ii) tuberculosis or any infectious disease to which regulation 9 of the Public Health (Aircraft) Regulations 1979 (powers in respect of persons leaving aircraft) applies or to which regulation 10 of the Public Health (Ships) Regulations 1979 (powers in respect of certain persons on ships) applies; and
-- src:2784 | (b) in Scotland any—
-- src:2785 | (i) infectious disease within the meaning of section 1(5) of the Public Health etc (Scotland) Act 2008 , or exposure to an organism causing that disease; or
-- src:2786 | (ii) contamination within the meaning of section 1(5) of that Act, or exposure to a contaminant,
-- src:2787 | to which sections 56 to 58 of that Act (compensation) apply.
@ref Sch 8 para 3 (src:2775-2787)
DECLARE `Sch 8 para 3 facts` HAS
    `nation in which the claimant is`                                                                                                IS A `Nation of Great Britain`
    `excluded or abstains from work pursuant to a request or notice in writing lawfully made or given under an enactment`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `otherwise prevented from working pursuant to an enactment`                                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is known or reasonably suspected that the claimant is infected or contaminated, or has been in contact with a case`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `incidence or spread of infection or contamination within section 45A(3) of the Public Health (Control of Disease) Act 1984 for which regulations are made under Part 2A of that Act`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `tuberculosis or an infectious disease to which regulation 9 of the Public Health (Aircraft) Regulations 1979 or regulation 10 of the Public Health (Ships) Regulations 1979 applies`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `infectious disease within section 1(5) of the Public Health etc (Scotland) Act 2008, or exposure to an organism causing that disease`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `contamination within section 1(5) of that Act, or exposure to a contaminant`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `sections 56 to 58 of the Public Health etc (Scotland) Act 2008 (compensation) apply to it`                                       IS A BOOLEAN

-- The closing words "to which sections 56 to 58 of that Act (compensation) apply" are set below both Scottish limbs, so they are
-- read as qualifying both (fork F-sch8-3).
@ref Sch 8 para 3(2) (src:2780-2787)
GIVEN facts IS A `Sch 8 para 3 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 8 para 3(2) — a relevant infection or contamination` facts MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `nation in which the claimant is`
    WHEN England  THEN `Sch 8 para 3(2)(a) — in England and Wales` facts
    WHEN Wales    THEN `Sch 8 para 3(2)(a) — in England and Wales` facts
    WHEN Scotland THEN `Sch 8 para 3(2)(b) — in Scotland` facts

@ref Sch 8 para 3(2)(a) (src:2781-2783)
GIVEN facts IS A `Sch 8 para 3 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 8 para 3(2)(a) — in England and Wales` facts MEANS
    (facts's `incidence or spread of infection or contamination within section 45A(3) of the Public Health (Control of Disease) Act 1984 for which regulations are made under Part 2A of that Act`)
    OR (facts's `tuberculosis or an infectious disease to which regulation 9 of the Public Health (Aircraft) Regulations 1979 or regulation 10 of the Public Health (Ships) Regulations 1979 applies`)

@ref Sch 8 para 3(2)(b) (src:2784-2787)
GIVEN facts IS A `Sch 8 para 3 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 8 para 3(2)(b) — in Scotland` facts MEANS
    (`disease or contamination`)
    AND (facts's `sections 56 to 58 of the Public Health etc (Scotland) Act 2008 (compensation) apply to it`)
    WHERE
        `disease or contamination` MEANS
            (facts's `infectious disease within section 1(5) of the Public Health etc (Scotland) Act 2008, or exposure to an organism causing that disease`)
            OR (facts's `contamination within section 1(5) of that Act, or exposure to a contaminant`)

@ref Sch 8 para 3(1) (src:2776-2779)
GIVEN facts IS A `Sch 8 para 3 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 8 para 3 — prevented from working by law` facts MEANS
    (`excluded or prevented`)
    AND (facts's `it is known or reasonably suspected that the claimant is infected or contaminated, or has been in contact with a case`)
    AND (`Sch 8 para 3(2) — a relevant infection or contamination` facts)
    WHERE
        `excluded or prevented` MEANS
            (facts's `excluded or abstains from work pursuant to a request or notice in writing lawfully made or given under an enactment`)
            OR (facts's `otherwise prevented from working pursuant to an enactment`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Paragraph 4 — Risk to self or others`

-- src:2788 | Risk to self or others
-- src:2789 | 4 (1) The claimant is suffering from a specific illness, disease or disablement by reason of which there would be a substantial risk to the physical or mental health of any person were the claimant found not to have limited capability for work.
-- src:2790 | (2) This paragraph does not apply where the risk could be reduced by a significant amount by—
-- src:2791 | (a) reasonable adjustments being made in the claimant's workplace; or
-- src:2792 | (b) the claimant taking medication to manage their condition where such medication has been prescribed for the claimant by a registered medical practitioner treating the claimant.
@ref Sch 8 para 4 (src:2788-2792)
DECLARE `Sch 8 para 4 risk facts` HAS
    `suffering from a specific illness, disease or disablement`                                                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `by reason of it there would be a substantial risk to the physical or mental health of any person were the claimant found not to have limited capability for work`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the risk could be reduced by a significant amount by reasonable adjustments being made in the claimant's workplace`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the risk could be reduced by a significant amount by the claimant taking medication prescribed by a registered medical practitioner treating the claimant`   IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Sch 8 para 4 (src:2789-2792)
GIVEN facts IS A `Sch 8 para 4 risk facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 8 para 4 — risk to self or others` facts MEANS
    (facts's `suffering from a specific illness, disease or disablement`)
    AND (facts's `by reason of it there would be a substantial risk to the physical or mental health of any person were the claimant found not to have limited capability for work`)
    AND (NOT (facts's `the risk could be reduced by a significant amount by reasonable adjustments being made in the claimant's workplace`))
    AND (NOT (facts's `the risk could be reduced by a significant amount by the claimant taking medication prescribed by a registered medical practitioner treating the claimant`))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Paragraph 5 — Life threatening disease`

-- src:2793 | Life threatening disease
-- src:2794 | 5 The claimant is suffering from a life threatening disease in relation to which—
-- src:2795 | (a) there is medical evidence that the disease is uncontrollable, or uncontrolled, by a recognised therapeutic procedure; and
-- src:2796 | (b) in the case of a disease that is uncontrolled, there is a reasonable cause for it not to be controlled by a recognised therapeutic procedure.
@ref Sch 8 para 5 (src:2793-2796)
DECLARE `Sch 8 para 5 disease facts` HAS
    `suffering from a life threatening disease`                                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is medical evidence that the disease is uncontrollable by a recognised therapeutic procedure`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is medical evidence that the disease is uncontrolled by a recognised therapeutic procedure`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is a reasonable cause for the disease not to be controlled by a recognised therapeutic procedure`   IS A BOOLEAN

-- Limb (b) bites only "in the case of a disease that is uncontrolled": if the disease is not uncontrolled it is satisfied.
@ref Sch 8 para 5 (src:2794-2796)
GIVEN facts IS A `Sch 8 para 5 disease facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 8 para 5 — life threatening disease` facts MEANS
    (facts's `suffering from a life threatening disease`)
    AND `limb a`
    AND `limb b`
    WHERE
        `limb a` MEANS
            (facts's `there is medical evidence that the disease is uncontrollable by a recognised therapeutic procedure`)
            OR (facts's `there is medical evidence that the disease is uncontrolled by a recognised therapeutic procedure`)
        `limb b` MEANS
            (NOT (facts's `there is medical evidence that the disease is uncontrolled by a recognised therapeutic procedure`))
            OR (facts's `there is a reasonable cause for the disease not to be controlled by a recognised therapeutic procedure`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Paragraph 6 — Disabled and over the age for state pension credit`

-- out of range: the qualifying age for state pension credit (not among the inputs): whether the claimant has reached it is a stated input
-- src:2797 | Disabled and over the age for state pension credit
-- src:2798 | 6 The claimant has reached the qualifying age for state pension credit and is entitled to disability living allowance , Scottish adult disability living allowance , personal independence payment or adult disability payment.
@ref Sch 8 para 6 (src:2797-2798)
DECLARE `Sch 8 para 6 facts` HAS
    `reached the qualifying age for state pension credit`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `entitled to`                                           IS A LIST OF Benefit

@ref Sch 8 para 6 (src:2798)
GIVEN facts IS A `Sch 8 para 6 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 8 para 6 — disabled and over the age for state pension credit` facts MEANS
    (facts's `reached the qualifying age for state pension credit`)
    AND `entitled to one of the four`
    WHERE
        `entitled to one of the four` MEANS
            (elem `disability living allowance` (facts's `entitled to`))
            OR (elem `Scottish adult disability living allowance` (facts's `entitled to`))
            OR (elem `personal independence payment` (facts's `entitled to`))
            OR (elem `adult disability payment` (facts's `entitled to`))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 39(6) and (7) — treated as having limited capability for work`

-- src:762 | (6) Subject to paragraph (7), a claimant is to be treated as having limited capability for work if any of the circumstances set out in Schedule 8 applies.
-- src:763 | (7) Where the circumstances set out in paragraph 4 or 5 of Schedule 8 apply, a claimant may only be treated as having limited capability for work if the claimant does not have limited capability for work as determined in accordance with an assessment under this Part.
@ref reg 39(6) and (7) (src:762-763)
DECLARE `Sch 8 circumstances` HAS
    `paragraph 1 facts`  IS A `Sch 8 para 1 treatment facts`
    `paragraph 2 facts`  IS A `Sch 8 para 2 hospital facts`
    `paragraph 3 facts`  IS A `Sch 8 para 3 facts`
    `paragraph 4 facts`  IS A `Sch 8 para 4 risk facts`
    `paragraph 5 facts`  IS A `Sch 8 para 5 disease facts`
    `paragraph 6 facts`  IS A `Sch 8 para 6 facts`

-- Paragraphs 4 and 5 only count where the claimant does not have limited capability for work as determined in accordance
-- with an assessment under Part 5 (paragraph (7)). That determination is the second input.
@ref reg 39(6) and (7) (src:762-763)
GIVEN circumstances IS A `Sch 8 circumstances`
      `limited capability for work as determined in accordance with an assessment under Part 5` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 39(6) and (7) — the claimant is to be treated as having limited capability for work` circumstances `limited capability for work as determined in accordance with an assessment under Part 5` MEANS
    `unrestricted paragraphs`
    OR `restricted paragraphs where paragraph seven allows`
    WHERE
        `unrestricted paragraphs` MEANS
            (`Sch 8 para 1 — receiving certain treatments` (circumstances's `paragraph 1 facts`))
            OR (`Sch 8 para 2 — in hospital` (circumstances's `paragraph 2 facts`))
            OR (`Sch 8 para 3 — prevented from working by law` (circumstances's `paragraph 3 facts`))
            OR (`Sch 8 para 6 — disabled and over the age for state pension credit` (circumstances's `paragraph 6 facts`))
        `restricted paragraphs where paragraph seven allows` MEANS
            (   (`Sch 8 para 4 — risk to self or others` (circumstances's `paragraph 4 facts`))
             OR (`Sch 8 para 5 — life threatening disease` (circumstances's `paragraph 5 facts`)))
            AND (NOT `limited capability for work as determined in accordance with an assessment under Part 5`)

-- =========================================================================================================
§ `Schedule 9 — Circumstances in which a claimant is to be treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity`

-- src:2799 | SCHEDULE 9 — Circumstances in which a claimant is to be treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Paragraph 1 — Terminal illness`

-- src:2800 | Terminal illness
-- src:2801 | 1 The claimant is terminally ill.
@ref Sch 9 para 1 (src:2800-2801)
GIVEN illness IS AN Illness
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 9 para 1 — terminal illness` illness MEANS
    `reg 2 — terminally ill` illness

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Paragraph 2 — Pregnancy`

-- src:2802 | Pregnancy
-- src:2803 | 2 The claimant is a pregnant woman and there is a serious risk of damage to her health or to the health of her unborn child if she does not refrain from work and work-related activity.
@ref Sch 9 para 2 (src:2802-2803)
DECLARE `Sch 9 para 2 pregnancy facts` HAS
    `a pregnant woman`                                                                                                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is a serious risk of damage to her health or to the health of her unborn child if she does not refrain from work and work-related activity`  IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Sch 9 para 2 (src:2803)
GIVEN facts IS A `Sch 9 para 2 pregnancy facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 9 para 2 — pregnancy` facts MEANS
    (facts's `a pregnant woman`)
    AND (facts's `there is a serious risk of damage to her health or to the health of her unborn child if she does not refrain from work and work-related activity`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Paragraph 3 — Receiving treatment for cancer`

-- src:2804 | Receiving treatment for cancer
-- src:2805 | 3 The claimant is—
-- src:2806 | (a) receiving treatment for cancer by way of chemotherapy or radiotherapy;
-- src:2807 | (b) likely to receive such treatment within 6 months after the date of the determination of capability for work and work-related activity; or
-- src:2808 | (c) recovering from such treatment,
-- src:2809 | and the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant should be treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity.
@ref Sch 9 para 3 (src:2804-2809)
DECLARE `Sch 9 para 3 cancer treatment facts` HAS
    `receiving treatment for cancer by way of chemotherapy or radiotherapy`                                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `likely to receive such treatment within 6 months after the date of the determination of capability for work and work-related activity`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `recovering from such treatment`                                                                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant should be treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- The closing words "and the Secretary of State is satisfied that ..." stand below limbs (a) to (c) and after "or", so they
-- are read as qualifying all three limbs (fork F-sch9-1). Compare Sch 8 para 1, where the same satisfaction qualifies only
-- the recovering limb because it is written inside that limb.
@ref Sch 9 para 3 (src:2805-2809)
GIVEN facts IS A `Sch 9 para 3 cancer treatment facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 9 para 3 — receiving treatment for cancer` facts MEANS
    `in one of the three situations`
    AND (facts's `the Secretary of State is satisfied that the claimant should be treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity`)
    WHERE
        `in one of the three situations` MEANS
            (facts's `receiving treatment for cancer by way of chemotherapy or radiotherapy`)
            OR (facts's `likely to receive such treatment within 6 months after the date of the determination of capability for work and work-related activity`)
            OR (facts's `recovering from such treatment`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Paragraph 4 — Risk to self or others`

-- src:2810 | Risk to self or others
-- src:2811 | 4 The claimant is suffering from a specific illness, disease or disablement by reason of which there would be a substantial risk to the physical or mental health of any person were the claimant found not to have limited capability for work and work-related activity.
@ref Sch 9 para 4 (src:2810-2811)
DECLARE `Sch 9 para 4 risk facts` HAS
    `suffering from a specific illness, disease or disablement`                                                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `by reason of it there would be a substantial risk to the physical or mental health of any person were the claimant found not to have limited capability for work and work-related activity`  IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Sch 9 para 4 (src:2811)
GIVEN facts IS A `Sch 9 para 4 risk facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 9 para 4 — risk to self or others` facts MEANS
    (facts's `suffering from a specific illness, disease or disablement`)
    AND (facts's `by reason of it there would be a substantial risk to the physical or mental health of any person were the claimant found not to have limited capability for work and work-related activity`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Paragraph 5 — Disabled and over the age for state pension credit`

-- out of range: the qualifying age for state pension credit (not among the inputs): whether the claimant has reached it is a stated input
-- src:2812 | Disabled and over the age for state pension credit
-- src:2813 | 5 The claimant has reached the qualifying age for state pension credit and is entitled to attendance allowance , pension age disability payment, the care component of disability living allowance at the highest rate , the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025 or the daily living component of personal independence payment at the enhanced rate or the daily living component of adult disability payment at the enhanced rate in accordance with regulation 5(3) of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022.
@ref Sch 9 para 5 (src:2812-2813)
DECLARE `Sch 9 para 5 facts` HAS
    `reached the qualifying age for state pension credit`                                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `entitled to`                                                                                                          IS A LIST OF Benefit
    `entitled to the care component of disability living allowance at the highest rate`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `entitled to the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `entitled to the daily living component of personal independence payment at the enhanced rate`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `entitled to the daily living component of adult disability payment at the enhanced rate in accordance with regulation 5(3) of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022`   IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Sch 9 para 5 (src:2813)
GIVEN facts IS A `Sch 9 para 5 facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 9 para 5 — disabled and over the age for state pension credit` facts MEANS
    (facts's `reached the qualifying age for state pension credit`)
    AND `entitled to one of the six`
    WHERE
        `entitled to one of the six` MEANS
            (elem `attendance allowance` (facts's `entitled to`))
            OR (elem `pension age disability payment` (facts's `entitled to`))
            OR (facts's `entitled to the care component of disability living allowance at the highest rate`)
            OR (facts's `entitled to the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025`)
            OR (facts's `entitled to the daily living component of personal independence payment at the enhanced rate`)
            OR (facts's `entitled to the daily living component of adult disability payment at the enhanced rate in accordance with regulation 5(3) of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Regulation 40(5) and (6) — treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity`

-- src:782 | (5) Subject to paragraph (6), a claimant is to be treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity if any of the circumstances set out in Schedule 9 applies.
-- src:783 | (6) Where the circumstances set out in paragraph 4 of Schedule 9 apply, a claimant may only be treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity if the claimant does not have limited capability for work and work-related activity as determined in accordance with an assessment under this Part.
@ref reg 40(5) and (6) (src:782-783)
DECLARE `Sch 9 circumstances` HAS
    `paragraph 1 facts`  IS AN Illness
    `paragraph 2 facts`  IS A `Sch 9 para 2 pregnancy facts`
    `paragraph 3 facts`  IS A `Sch 9 para 3 cancer treatment facts`
    `paragraph 4 facts`  IS A `Sch 9 para 4 risk facts`
    `paragraph 5 facts`  IS A `Sch 9 para 5 facts`

-- Paragraph 4 only counts where the claimant does not have limited capability for work and work-related activity as
-- determined in accordance with an assessment under Part 5 (paragraph (6)).
@ref reg 40(5) and (6) (src:782-783)
GIVEN circumstances IS A `Sch 9 circumstances`
      `limited capability for work and work-related activity as determined in accordance with an assessment under Part 5` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 40(5) and (6) — the claimant is to be treated as having limited capability for work and work-related activity` circumstances `limited capability for work and work-related activity as determined in accordance with an assessment under Part 5` MEANS
    `unrestricted paragraphs`
    OR `restricted paragraph where paragraph six allows`
    WHERE
        `unrestricted paragraphs` MEANS
            (`Sch 9 para 1 — terminal illness` (circumstances's `paragraph 1 facts`))
            OR (`Sch 9 para 2 — pregnancy` (circumstances's `paragraph 2 facts`))
            OR (`Sch 9 para 3 — receiving treatment for cancer` (circumstances's `paragraph 3 facts`))
            OR (`Sch 9 para 5 — disabled and over the age for state pension credit` (circumstances's `paragraph 5 facts`))
        `restricted paragraph where paragraph six allows` MEANS
            (`Sch 9 para 4 — risk to self or others` (circumstances's `paragraph 4 facts`))
            AND (NOT `limited capability for work and work-related activity as determined in accordance with an assessment under Part 5`)
